  "voice set: no tool writes a new voice (talk.set phrase lines + sound/human/talk/<id>/ tree): gen op `voice` {id, like, speakers, sounds:{<event>: folder}} that copies the like language tree into the mod, adds (\"phrase_voice\" <talk> <id> N <folder>) lines to a mod talk.set \"phrases\" define, optional breed link",
  "events: per-event line choice (which folder or files per moment) has no writer: part of gen `voice` sounds map, sound files through /api/x/art/sound",
  "events: 16 engine events are silent in vanilla (ally die, explosion, cannot move ...): gen `voice` events:{name: folder} adds a new {talk} block [T]",
  "phrase: freq per talk block has no writer: gen `voice` freq:{event: f} (it changes every voice, so mod talk.set copy)",
  "phrase: shown text (text key talk/<key>) has no writer apart from gen text; gen `voice` text:{event: words} writes key and lang rows",
  "sound: folder.set tag, loudness, volume, distance have no writer: gen `voice` folder:{loudness, volume} writes folder.set in the new tree",
  "schedule: set/talk/<talker>/*.set situation rules have no writer: gen op `talk-rule` {talker, talk, priority, timeout, immediate, condition}",
  "shared: sound.set loudness/percent rows have no writer (change all talk): keep, list in kept",
  "link: breed voice is settable (gen breed set:+voice) but nothing checks the id exists in talk.set: a gen check that the voice id has phrase lines"
 ]
